---
import DocsLayout from "../../../components/DocsLayout.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../../../components/CodeBlock.astro";

const read = `import { isMdbaseError, toPlain } from "@mdbase-dev/sdk";

// By ID, or by path. get() throws not_found; find() returns null.
const task = await db.get({ path: "tasks/plan.md" }, { body: true });
const maybe = await db.find(taskId);

console.log(task.revision);                   // "sha256:…"
console.log(toPlain(task.frontmatter));       // plain object
console.log(task.state.state);                // "confirmed" or "pending"

// One page of a query. Pass page.cursor to get the next.
const page = await db.query({
  types: ["task"],
  where: 'status != "done"',
  order_by: [{ field: "due", direction: "asc" }],
  limit: 50,
});

// Or every page in turn.
for await (const p of db.pages({ types: ["task"], limit: 200 })) {
  render(p.records);
}`;

const live = `const open = db.live(
  { types: ["task"], where: 'status == "open"', limit: 100 },
  { effective: true },
);

const stop = open.subscribe((state) => {
  // Called now, then after every snapshot, diff or reset.
  renderList(state.records, { stale: state.stale });
});

// Widen the window later without a new subscription.
await open.setQuery({ types: ["task"], where: 'status == "open"', limit: 200 });

// When the screen closes:
stop();
open.close();`;

const write = `const created = await db.create({
  type: "task",
  path: "tasks/review.md",
  frontmatter: { title: "Review the draft", status: "open" },
  body: "Check the numbers.\\n",
});
const id = created.records[0].id; // usable straight away

// Pass the record you read. Only the fields you change are sent, each with
// the value you saw, so concurrent edits to other fields merge.
const task = await db.get(id, { body: true });
await db.update(task, {
  patch: { status: "in-progress" },
  add: { tags: ["review"] },
  body: task.body + "Add a summary.\\n",
});

await db.rename(task, "tasks/review-q3.md"); // updates links by default
await db.delete(id);`;

const changes = `let cursor = loadCursor();

const watch = db.watchChanges(cursor, (batch) => {
  if (batch.reset) {
    rebuildFromScratch(); // the cursor expired: start again
  } else {
    applyChanges(batch.changes);
  }
  saveCursor(batch.cursor);
});
await watch.ready;

// Later:
watch();`;

const preflight = `const preview = await db.update(task, { patch: { status: "done" } }, { dryRun: true });
console.log(preview.receipt.preflight);

const issues = await db.validate([{ path: "tasks/review.md" }]);`;
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Records and operations"
  description="Read, query, watch, create, update, rename and delete records. Writes are optimistic and merge field by field."
  active="operations"
  headings={[
    { href: "#outcomes", label: "Records and errors" },
    { href: "#read-query", label: "Read and query" },
    { href: "#live", label: "Live queries" },
    { href: "#write", label: "Write" },
    { href: "#preconditions", label: "Preconditions" },
    { href: "#watch", label: "Watch changes" },
    { href: "#preflight", label: "Check before writing" },
    { href: "#files", label: "Attachments" }
  ]}
>
  <p>
    All examples use <code>db</code>, an <code>MdbaseClient</code> from
    {" "}<code>connect()</code> or from an app connection’s
    {" "}<code>records</code>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="outcomes">Records and errors</h2>
  <p>
    A record is a <code>RecordView</code>: <code>id</code>, <code>path</code>,
    {" "}<code>revision</code>, <code>types</code>, <code>frontmatter</code>
    {" "}(a <code>Map</code>), and <code>state</code>. Ask for more with the
    {" "}<code>include</code> argument: <code>body</code>,
    {" "}<code>effective</code> (values with type defaults applied),
    {" "}<code>document</code>, <code>links</code> and
    {" "}<code>diagnostics</code>.
  </p>
  <p>
    Failures throw <code>MdbaseError</code>. Check them with
    {" "}<code>isMdbaseError(e, code)</code>. Each error has a
    {" "}<code>code</code>, a <code>recovery</code> that says what to do, and
    often a <code>reason</code>. The full list is in the
    {" "}<a href="/sdk/api/#errors">API reference</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="read-query">Read and query</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={read} language="ts" label="read.ts" />
  <p>
    Queries use the <a href="/spec/">mdbase query format</a>:
    {" "}<code>types</code>, <code>where</code>, <code>order_by</code>,
    {" "}<code>select</code>, <code>limit</code> and more. Reads answer from
    the replica’s local view, including your pending writes.
  </p>
  <p>
    A cursor can expire. <code>pages()</code> then throws
    {" "}<code>invalid_request</code> with reason <code>cursor_expired</code>
    {" "}or <code>cursor_stale</code>. Pass <code>&#123; onReset &#125;</code>
    {" "}as its fourth argument to restart from the first page instead; clear
    what you collected when it is called.
  </p>

  <h2 id="live">Live queries</h2>
  <p>
    A live query keeps its result current. The replica sends a snapshot, then
    a diff for each change.
  </p>
  <CodeBlock code={live} language="ts" label="task-list.ts" />
  <p>
    Keep live lists cheap: use a <code>limit</code> window and leave bodies
    out. <code>state.stale</code> is true until the first snapshot and after
    a reset; the previous records stay visible meanwhile.
  </p>

  <h2 id="write">Write</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={write} language="ts" label="write.ts" />
  <p>
    Every write returns a <code>Write</code> at once, in the
    {" "}<code>pending</code> state. Your reads and live queries show it
    straight away. Await <code>write.confirmed</code> if you need to know the
    log accepted it; see <a href="/sdk/offline-sync/">Pending writes and sync status</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    When you pass a <code>RecordView</code> to <code>update()</code>, the SDK
    sends the values you saw with the fields you change. A new body is sent as
    edits against the body you read and merged with other changes. Patch keys
    whose value didn’t change are dropped, so they can’t cause conflicts.
  </p>
  <p>
    <code>replaceDocument(record, source)</code> replaces the whole Markdown
    source when you need to. For a screen where people type into a record, use
    a <a href="/sdk/editing/">record session</a> instead.
  </p>

  <h2 id="preconditions">Preconditions</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <code>ifRevision: record.revision</code> applies the write only if the
      record is still at that revision. Otherwise it is rejected with
      {" "}<code>conflict</code> and reason <code>revision</code>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <code>conflictMode: "reject"</code> in the write options rejects the
      whole write if any part of it conflicts. The default,
      {" "}<code>"record"</code>, applies what merges and records the rest as
      conflicts.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="watch">Watch changes</h2>
  <p>
    The change feed lists what changed since a cursor. Use it to keep an
    index or an export up to date.
  </p>
  <CodeBlock code={changes} language="ts" label="changes.ts" />
  <p>
    An expired cursor gives <code>reset: true</code>, not an error.
    {" "}<code>db.changes(cursor, limit)</code> reads one batch without
    watching.
  </p>

  <h2 id="preflight">Check before writing</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={preflight} language="ts" label="preflight.ts" />
  <p>
    <code>dryRun: true</code> runs every check without writing.
    {" "}<code>preflightRename()</code> and <code>preflightDelete()</code> show
    what a rename or delete would touch, such as links in other records.
    {" "}<code>validate()</code> checks records against their types.
  </p>

  <h2 id="files">Attachments</h2>
  <p>
    Files that aren’t records, such as images and PDFs, use
    {" "}<code>db.files</code>.
  </p>
  <CodeBlock code={`const upload = await db.files.upload("attachments/plan.pdf", file, {
  onProgress: (p) => showProgress(p),
});
await upload.confirmed; // the bytes are stored

const bytes = await db.files.download({ path: "attachments/plan.pdf" });

for await (const f of db.files.list()) {
  console.log(f.path, f.size, f.state); // state: "materialized", "remote", …
}`} language="ts" label="files.ts" />
  <ul>
    <li>
      Uploads go in 1 MiB chunks. To resume an interrupted upload, call
      {" "}<code>upload()</code> again with the same <code>transferId</code>.
      Pass <code>fileId</code> to replace an existing file.
    </li>
    <li>
      <code>download()</code> reads up to 64 MiB into memory. For anything
      larger, use <code>downloadStream()</code>, which also takes a byte
      <code>range</code>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <code>move()</code> and <code>delete()</code> take
      {" "}<code>ifRevision</code>, like records.
    </li>
  </ul>
</DocsLayout>
